Ta có: $1 - 2 \sin^2(2x) = \cos \left(3x - \dfrac{\pi}{4} \right)$
$\Leftrightarrow \cos(4x) = \cos \left(3x - \dfrac{\pi}{4} \right)$
$\Leftrightarrow \left[
\begin{array}{l}
4x = 3x - \dfrac{\pi}{4} + k2\pi\\
4x = -3x + \dfrac{\pi}{4} + k2\pi
\end{array}
\right.$
$\Leftrightarrow \left[
\begin{array}{l}
x = -\dfrac{\pi}{4} + k2\pi\\
7x = \dfrac{\pi}{4} + k2\pi
\end{array}
\right.$
$\Leftrightarrow \left[
\begin{array}{l}
x = -\dfrac{\pi}{4} + k2\pi\\
x = \dfrac{\pi}{28} + \dfrac{k2\pi}{7}
\end{array}
\right. \quad (k \in \mathbb{Z})$
